From d0bd34024d3f16b1cbeb1b8938cbfec37aa16dac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:44:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] feat(inkling2): --vision-upscale enlarges an image before
 the vision tower's token budget bounds it

Inkling 2's tower takes an image at its own resolution in 40-pixel cells, so screen text whose glyphs are smaller
than a 20-pixel patch reached it unreadable. --vision-upscale F (1 to 4, default 1: unchanged behaviour; Inkling 2
only, other families refuse another value) enlarges each side by F, in whole cells, before the existing
--vision-max-merged bound; an image already at the budget is unchanged.

On a local probe (dense UI text and code screenshots, RTX 5080) 1.5 read every line where 1.0 missed some; a
1920 x 1080 screenshot then takes 3,013 positions instead of 1,357. Options plumbing for ninfer and ninfer-serve,
docs/cli.md, docs/serving.md and the family guide are updated.

Not done: the repository test suite was not run, no frontend test for the new resize bound, and no README What's New item.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
